  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Child Protection In Emergencies and GBV services to upscale protection of boys, girls and Adolescents from risks of Violence, Abuse, Neglect and Exploitation in Torit and Pibor counties - Eastern Equatoria and Jonglei States</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PI, through UNICEF support, has implemented CPiE services in Pibor and Torit since 2020, and will continue contributing to improved protective environment and coping mechanisms of children and families. 
Project Outcome&amp;#58;
&#x2022;	Targeted girls and boys and youth in humanitarian situations provided with psychosocial support, through child friendly spaces, schools and other community spaces 
&#x2022;	Targeted unaccompanied and separated girls and boys registered with family tracing and reunification services and family-based care or appropriate alternative services 
&#x2022;	Extremely vulnerable children including unaccompanied and separated children reached with individual comprehensive and age-specific case management services.</narrative>
  </description>
